      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I think that's a great idea, but what video service would that actually work for?\n\nFor video playback the system wants a combined video file, like audio and video in the same file. \n\nFor youtube this typically means 720p, most of the quality levels are separate.\n\nMaybe it'd work for twitch if the particular creator is big enough?\n\nPointing at a video file on a server, resolution limit won't apply there either.",
